<title>POLAND: LUBAWA PLANS TO PAY 1996 DIVIDEND.</title>
<headline>LUBAWA PLANS TO PAY 1996 DIVIDEND.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shareholders of Polish technical garment maker Lubawa SA will vote at a general meeting on March 22 on the size of the dividend the management plans to pay for 1996, the company said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The firm, whose full name is Zaklady Konfekcji Technicznej Lubawa SA, made a net profit of 1.8 million zlotys over the first 11 months of last year against 0.8 million zlotys in the same period in 1995.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
